# Prisma Schema Conventions

## Field naming: always map camelCase to snake_case

Every camelCase field **must** have an explicit `@map("snake_case")` annotation. The database column is always snake_case; the Prisma model field is always camelCase.

```prisma
// ❌ BAD — missing @map, column will be camelCase in DB
model Game {
  statsProcessed Boolean @default(false)
  homeTeamId     String
}

// ✅ GOOD
model Game {
  statsProcessed Boolean @default(false) @map("stats_processed")
  homeTeamId     String  @map("home_team_id")
}
```

## Model naming: always map PascalCase to snake_case table name

```prisma
// ❌ BAD
model PlayoffSeries { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
model PlayoffSeries {
  ...
  @@map("playoff_series")
}
```

## Relation fields

Bare relation fields (no column in DB) do **not** get `@map` — only scalar FK fields do.

```prisma
model Game {
  playoffSeriesId String?        @map("playoff_series_id")  // ✅ scalar FK → @map
  playoffSeries   PlayoffSeries? @relation(...)              // ✅ relation field → no @map
}
```

## Timestamps

All timestamp fields must use `@map`:

```prisma
createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at")
updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt      @map("updated_at")
```
